WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.277
A double-bar graph places paired values side by side for comparison. Always read both

00:00:05.277 --> 00:00:06.728
axes and the key.

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:13.222
One bar shows 30 and another 18. What is the difference? The answer is 12. Compare

00:00:13.222 --> 00:00:16.067
the two bars: |30 minus 18| equals 12.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:22.132
Two bars in a recycling club show Class A equals 29 and Class B equals 10. Which

00:00:22.132 --> 00:00:25.229
class has the taller bar? Pause the video and think.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:31.443
Two bars in a recycling club show Class A equals 29 and Class B equals 10. Which

00:00:31.443 --> 00:00:36.853
class has the taller bar? The answer is Class A. The larger bar is 29, belonging to

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:37.489
Class A.
